llama.cpp and ggml: compiled into the Linux and macOS apps, which run Sloane's model in their own process
=========================================================================================================

The Linux app of Crimson Noir: Agent City (its .deb, .rpm and AppImage) and its macOS app (the universal .app, in its
.dmg and its zip), built by .github/workflows/build-matrix.yml with the cargo feature native-runner, run the model
they carry in their own process: llama.cpp's model library (libllama) and ggml (ggml, ggml-base and ggml-cpu, and on
Apple silicon ggml-metal) are compiled from source and linked statically into the app's executable, through the Rust
crates llama-cpp-2 and llama-cpp-sys-2 0.1.161 (from crates.io; the llama-cpp-rs repository at commit
e7af607ebd5ec2932709ef918c17cca2f9b0fce4), which vendor llama.cpp's sources. In the macOS app's Apple silicon slice
ggml's Metal backend is compiled in with its shader sources embedded in the executable; its Intel slice is built
without Metal. Nothing of llama.cpp is in this repository: the sources come from the crate in the build's cargo
registry. The Windows, Android and iOS builds, the page file and the OS media do not compile it.

LICENSE beside this file is llama.cpp's own licence text, exactly as the vendored copy carries it (MIT License,
"Copyright (c) 2023-2026 The ggml authors"). The Linux packages install this NOTICE and that LICENSE as
/usr/share/doc/crimson-noir-agent-city/llama.cpp/NOTICE and LICENSE, and the macOS app holds them as
Contents/Resources/licenses/llama.cpp/NOTICE and LICENSE (src-tauri/tauri.model.conf.json).

What is compiled in, and under which terms
------------------------------------------

- llama.cpp and ggml, its Metal backend and shaders among them: MIT, Copyright (c) 2023-2026 The ggml authors
  (LICENSE beside this file).
- ggml's CPU matrix multiplication from llamafile (ggml/src/ggml-cpu/llamafile/sgemm.cpp): MIT, Copyright 2024
  Mozilla Foundation, under the same permission notice as LICENSE, which the file's own header carries.
- ggml's YaRN rotary scaling (ggml/src/ggml-cpu/ops.cpp, rope_yarn): MIT, Copyright (c) 2023 Jeffrey Quesnelle and
  Bowen Peng, as the code's own comment says.
- The Rust crates llama-cpp-2 and llama-cpp-sys-2: MIT OR Apache-2.0 (the crates' manifests); the product takes them
  under MIT.

The app links none of the download, Hugging Face cache, HTTP or subprocess code of llama.cpp's common library, no
cpp-httplib, no OpenSSL and no curl: tools/build/linuxAudit.mjs (symbols) checks it on every Linux build, and
tools/build/macAudit.mjs (symbols) on every macOS build, slice by slice, from the linker's map and the binary, and
each fails the build otherwise.

The software remains under its own licence, not under the product's licence. "llama.cpp" is a name of its authors,
used here only to say which software this is.
